  "Header":           "CAE-ASM-V1.0",

  "APIProfile":       "Basic",

  "Description":      "Audio Scene Management. Audio Scene Editing executes every User Command: it opens or creates Basic Audio Objects and Audio Objects, edits them and composes Objects, composes Basic Audio Scenes and Audio Scenes and sets their User Point of View; every edit is a new version in the Module's Shared Storage, from which Objects and Scenes are opened by their identifiers. Capture, reading the User's stored Objects, and hearing Objects and Scenes - rendered from the User Point of View, and played - are the User Agent's, through the Units of its Physical Layer: the Module takes the Basic Audio Object the User Agent gives and gives back the open Object and the open Scene. Speech Translation: an Object Command naming Translated Objects has a Basic Speech Object translated by Text and Speech Translation (MMC-TST) into the language its Speech Qualifier states; the translation replaces the original, under its identifier, so every Scene holding it holds the translation, at its place.",

